Month = {SEP 15},
Abstract = {Let (A, B) be a GP-admissible pair and (Z, W) be a GIadmissible pair of
   classes of objects in an abelian category C, and consider the class pi
   GP((omega,B,1)) of 1-periodic (omega, B)-Gorenstein projective objects,
   where.:= A boolean AND B and v:= Z boolean AND W. We claimed in {[}9,
   Lem. 8.1] that the (Z, W)-Gorenstein injective dimension of pi
   GP((omega,B,1)) is bounded by the (Z, W)-Gorenstein injective dimension
   of., provided that: (1).is closed under direct summands, (2) Ext1(pi
   GP((omega,B,1)) , v) = 0, and (3) every object in pi GP((omega,B,1))
   admits a Hom(-,v)-acyclic v-coresolution. These conditions and their
   duals are part of what we called ``Setup 1{''}. Moreover, if we replace
   pi GP((omega,B,1)) by the class GP((A,B)) of (A, B)-Gorenstein
   projective objects, the resulting inequality is claimed to be true under
   a set of conditions named ``Setup 2{''}. The proof we gave for the
   claims Gid( Z,W)(pi GP((omega,B,1))) <= Gid((Z,W))(omega) and
   Gid((Z,W))(GP((A,B))) <= Gid((Z,W))(omega) is incorrect, and the purpose
   of this note is to exhibit a corrected proof of the first inequality,
   under the additional assumption that every object in pi GP((omega,B,1))
   has finite injective dimension relative to Z. Setup 2 is no longer
   required, and as a result the second inequality was removed. We also fix
   those results in 8 of {[}9] affected by Lemma 8.1, and comment some
   applications and examples. (c) 2024 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.},
