Abstract = {In this paper, we define some combinatorial principles to characterize
   spaces X whose hyperspace satisfies some variation of some classical
   star selection principle. Specifically, the variations characterized are
   the selective and absolute versions of the star selection principles for
   the Menger and Rothberger cases; also, the hyperspaces considered in
   these characterizations are CL(X), K(X), F(X) and CS(X) in both cases,
   endowed with either the Fell topology or the Vietoris topology. (c) 2024
   Mathematical Institute Slovak Academy of Sciences},
