Pages = {8-14},
Month = {MAY 10},
Abstract = {The family Amaranthaceae has a cosmopolitan distribution and it is one
   of the most diverse families within the order Caryo-phyllales. Species
   of Amaranthaceae live mainly in arid environments, saline habitats, or
   disturbed areas. Nomenclature is the necessary first-step to study the
   members of this group, aiming to clarify their identity which is often
   critical. The types of four names in Amaranthaceae (sensu lato,
   including Chenopodiaceae)-Chenopodium berlandieri, Celosia monosperma,
   Iresine grandis var. glabrata, Iresine interrupta-with Mexican loci
   classici are designated in the present paper, including comments on
   their identities.},
