Abstract = {{[} T 0 J In this paper we study the lower triangular matrix K-algebra
   \& ULambda; := , where M U U and T are basic K-algebras with enough
   idempotents and M is an U-T-bimodule where K acts centrally. Moreover,
   we characterise in terms of U, T and M when, on one hand, the lower
   triangular matrix K-algebra \& ULambda; is standardly stratified in the
   sense of {[}15]; and on the other hand, when \& ULambda; is locally
   bounded in the sense of Gabriel {[}10]. Finally, we also study several
   properties relating the projective dimensions in the categories of
   finitely generated modules mod(U), mod(T) and mod(\& ULambda;).(c) 2022
