Abstract = {This paper studies the selectively pseudocompact-open topology on the
   set of the real-valued continuous functions on a Tychonoff space, and
   compares this topology with the alpha-open topology and the topology of
   uniform convergence on the elements of alpha where alpha is one of the
   following: \{X\}, the finite subsets of X, the compact subsets of X, the
   countably compact subsets of X, and the pseudocompact subsets of X.
   Moreover, it also analyzes the almost cc-omega-bounded spaces.},
