   13-15, 2018},
Organization = {Natl Autonomous Univ Mexico, Complex Sci Ctr; Philips Healthcare;
   ScientyMed},
Abstract = {The BIOBEAM GM2000 irradiation system was originally designed for blood
   irradiation (doses starting from 25Gy). In order to utilize this system
   for cell culture irradiation in pre-clinical research (doses from 0.5 to
   2.5Gy), a detailed description of the dose distribution at the
   aforementioned range is needed. The dosimetry was performed using
   TLD-100 in conjunction with EBT3 radiochromic film. Our main goal was to
   establish a set of irradiation parameters which ensure that the intended
   dose is delivered to the cell cultures. As a result of this work, a
   software tool was developed so as to automate the plan creation process.
   This will allow the use of this device for pre-clinical cell culture
   irradiation.},
